  "integration": "Integrated in public/game-shell.js: the region picker opens five spacious region maps, map markers open existing scenes/cases, new interiors or short resident tips, and season/weather/time state is shared by map and room rendering. The art studio, arcade, woodshop, office and archive are enterable from their assigned NPCs and each has four clear-noon seasonal images. Indoor precipitation is clipped to each room's window areas. Nine pixel teacher sprites (librarian, smith, postman, doctor, painter, gamer, carpenter, archivist, clerk) and five pixel townspeople (fisher, kid, vendor, jogger, musician) use staggered short patrols with six-frame side-walk cycles in their assigned open areas. Six transparent pixel animal sheets each contain three four-frame action rows; the idle loop runs by default and clicking briefly plays that animal’s reaction row. Regional maps use click-to-travel hotspots; collision/pathfinding remains available only on the retained legacy town map. Pixel character sprites render with pixelated sampling.",
